 "meta": {
  "about": "Cases where the two expanders disagree. Unadjudicated unless referenced in findings/.",
  "dtstart_synchronized_cases": 12,
  "dtstart_unsynchronized_cases": 6,
  "first_period_truncation_note": "The 12 dtstart_synchronized cases share one shape and are analysed in findings/004-bysetpos-first-period-truncation.md: dateutil and rrule.js drop instances earlier than DTSTART before applying BYSETPOS, so BYSETPOS indexes a truncated set in DTSTART's own period. RFC 5545 3.3.10 says the set 'starts at the beginning of the interval defined by the FREQ rule part'. Recorded as a spec/practice divergence, not as 12 implementation bugs.",
  "rule_invalid_cases": 0,
  "rule_valid_cases": 18,
  "synchronization_note": "RFC 5545 sec 3.8.5.3 declares the recurrence set undefined when DTSTART is not synchronized with the recurrence rule. Cases with dtstart_synchronized=false record observed cross-implementation convention in that undefined region, NOT a conformance requirement. Consume them as interop data; do not cite them as spec violations.",
  "validity_note": "rule_valid is computed by src/validity.py from RFC 5545 3.3.10 MUST NOT constraints and value ranges, independently of any expander. It is a third, separate dimension: rule validity, DTSTART synchronization, and implementation agreement are different questions. Agreement on a rule the spec prohibits is not evidence of conformance."
 }
